# Portable visual notes

> [!TIP] A single file when you share
> Use Insert to add an image from your device or its HTTPS URL. Export portable
> `.fmd` to embed the images; Source mode still shows short Markdown references.

## Vector diagrams

```svg
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 540 130" width="540" height="130">
  <rect x="10" y="20" width="180" height="90" rx="18" fill="#e1ecff"/>
  <rect x="350" y="20" width="180" height="90" rx="18" fill="#e2f3ec"/>
  <path d="M210 65H325M308 48L325 65L308 82" fill="none" stroke="#42669e" stroke-width="4"/>
  <g font-family="sans-serif" font-size="20" text-anchor="middle" fill="#23334a">
    <text x="100" y="73">Clear source</text>
    <text x="440" y="73">Portable file</text>
  </g>
</svg>
```

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  Source --> Study --> Share
```

## Mathematics remains editable

$$
\int_0^1 x^2\,dx = \frac{1}{3}
$$

SVG and Mermaid export as clean vector diagrams. Interactive charts export as
static snapshots, while their slider source stays editable in `.fmd`.
